      "terms": "'NBA Live 99 Original 1998 Rosters' 1.0 (8 March 2017, uploaded by Andrew) from the NLSC's Downloads database: EA's own roster files from the NBA Live 99 PC CD-ROM (© EA Sports 1998), no licence given. The .7z (MD5 6280cd1d87748d80689c053037c028e0) is pinned as downloaded, and its PLAYERS.DBF and TEAMS.DBF as extracted; only those two dBase tables are read, as data. Because of the 1998 lockout the game shipped with the final 1997/98 rosters plus the trades of May and June 1998 and none of the 1998 draft; the season is 1998/99, the edition's, as NBA 2K12 carries 2011/12 on the lockout's 2010/11 rosters. Free agents and the All-Star teams are left out, and so is every player Basketball-Reference (check) does not have playing in the NBA: the made-up 'Roster Player' and a draft pick who never played. Each player keeps EA's computed overall (OVERALLRTG) as `raw`, put on NBA 2K's scale by `scale`.",
