      "scale": {
        "edition": "NBA 2K",
        "year": 2000,
        "intercept": 20.22,
        "slope": 1.089,
        "note": "NBA Live 99's overall is the rounded mean of 17 of its ratings, so it runs low (28-71 here) and undervalues specialists. One straight line puts it on NBA 2K's scale: the least-squares line of NBA 2K's overall (2K Archive's NBA 2K, 1999/00) on NBA Live 99's, through the players both editions rate, matched by name or alias. rating = round(20.22 + 1.089 × raw); its slope is positive, so no player passes another. The build fits the line again and stops if it is not this one. The audit gives every raw overall's rating and how the line does on those players."
